From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:54:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] avcodec/h264_slice: reset ref_pic_marking_bit_size for
 non-reference slices

Non-reference slices have no dec_ref_pic_marking() syntax, but the
field kept the size from the previous reference slice. V4L2 stateless
decoders get a stale dec_ref_pic_marking_bit_size for non-reference
B-frames.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 libavcodec/h264_slice.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/h264_slice.c b/libavcodec/h264_slice.c
index 9836aa3a7f..755222764f 100644
--- a/libavcodec/h264_slice.c
+++ b/libavcodec/h264_slice.c
@@ -1864,6 +1864,8 @@ static int h264_slice_header_parse(const H264Context *h, H264SliceContext *sl,
         if (ret < 0 && (h->avctx->err_recognition & AV_EF_EXPLODE))
             return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
         sl->ref_pic_marking_bit_size = pos - get_bits_left(&sl->gb);
+    } else {
+        sl->ref_pic_marking_bit_size = 0;
     }
 
     if (sl->slice_type_nos != AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I && pps->cabac) {
